\section*{The Bogoliubov momentum law for the dilute hard-sphere ground state}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. The hard-sphere ground state is claimed to have the full scaled Bogoliubov momentum law, with depletion $\frac{8}{3\sqrt\pi}\sqrt{\rho a^3}+o(\sqrt{\rho a^3})$.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Local energy estimates keep excitations instead of discarding them. One-body covariance and short-trajectory certificates are compared through smoothed deletion measures, while random encounter routes connect local momentum data to the thermodynamic occupation measure before the dilute limit.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
